{"tool_name":"bioconductor-scater","contents":["bioconductor","biocontainers","biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:bioconductor-scater","bioconductor:scater"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"bioconductor-scater","identifiers":["biotools:scater","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btw777"],"license":"GPL-3","summary":"Single-Cell Analysis Toolkit for Gene Expression Data in R","home_url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.11/bioc/html/scater.html","keywords":["Cell Line","Humans","Principal Component Analysis","Programming Languages","Quality Control","RNA","Sequence Analysis, RNA","Single-Cell Analysis","Statistics as Topic","RNA-seq","Quality affairs","Molecular genetics","Clustering","RNA-Seq","Transcriptomics","Gene Expression"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":3},"biotools":{"id":"bioconductor-scater","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/scater","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A collection of tools for doing various analyses of single-cell RNA-seq gene expression data, with a focus on quality control and visualization.","addition_date":"2026-09-01T07:30:05.330330Z","last_update_date":"2026-11-23T09:00:18.353102Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.40.2"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:bioconductor-scater","credit":[{"name":"Aaron Lun","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor","Developer"]},{"name":"Alan O'Callaghan","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor","Maintainer"]},{"name":"Davis McCarthy","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"Felix G.M. Ernst","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Kieran Campbell","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"Leo Lahti","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Quin Wills","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"Tuomas Borman","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Vladimir Kiselev","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Yun Peng","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/scater"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"name":"scater","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"gh2biotools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw777","metadata":{"abstract":"<h4>Motivation</h4>Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) is increasingly used to study gene expression at the level of individual cells. However, preparing raw sequence data for further analysis is not a straightforward process. Biases, artifacts and other sources of unwanted variation are present in the data, requiring substantial time and effort to be spent on pre-processing, quality control (QC) and normalization.<h4>Results</h4>We have developed the R/Bioconductor package scater to facilitate rigorous pre-processing, quality control, normalization and visualization of scRNA-seq data. The package provides a convenient, flexible workflow to process raw sequencing reads into a high-quality expression dataset ready for downstream analysis. scater provides a rich suite of plotting tools for single-cell data and a flexible data structure that is compatible with existing tools and can be used as infrastructure for future software development.<h4>Availability and implementation</h4>The open-source code, along with installation instructions, vignettes and case studies, is available through Bioconductor at http://bioconductor.org/packages/scater .<h4>Contact</h4>davis@ebi.ac.uk.<h4>Supplementary information</h4>Supplementary data are available at Bioinformatics online.","authors":[{"name":"Campbell KR"},{"name":"Lun AT"},{"name":"McCarthy DJ"},{"name":"Wills QF"}],"citationCount":1756,"date":"2017-04-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics (Oxford, England)","title":"Scater: pre-processing, quality control, normalization and visualization of single-cell RNA-seq data in R."},"pmcid":"PMC5408845","pmid":"28088763"}]},"biocon